  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\nc\\times (a+2b)=c\\times a+c\\times (2b)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\nc\\times a+c\\times (2b)=c\\times a+2(c\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $c\\times a$ and $c\\times b,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\times a+2(c\\times b) & =(3i-2j)+2(4i+j) \\\\  & =3i-2j+8i+2j \\\\  & =11\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
